# mix_audit 2.1.5 ignore list (docs/spec.md §11, §16).
#
# FORMAT: exactly one advisory ID per line, nothing else.
#   - Comments must start with "#" at column 0. A whitespace-prefixed "#" line
#     is parsed as an ID: it is harmless, but it is not a comment.
#   - Trailing whitespace or a CRLF ending silently disables that entry (lines
#     are split on "\n" and compared by exact string). This fails closed: the
#     un-ignored advisory is reported again.
#   - No wildcards and no package names exist. Ignoring an ID is narrower than
#     ignoring the package, so any new hackney advisory still fails.
# `--ignore-file` is the only file-backed key and 2.1.5 has no auto-discovery,
# so bare `mix deps.audit` ignores nothing. Run from the umbrella root (an
# app-local run finds no mix.lock and scans nothing):
#
#   mix deps.audit --ignore-file .mix_audit.ignore
#
# SCOPE: the audit reads every lockfile at the given root, so it covers the
# whole umbrella lock — dev/test-only packages included, not just prod deps.
#
# SILENT PASS: the advisory DB is a git clone at
# ~/.local/share/elixir-security-advisories-mirego that mix_audit refreshes
# with `git pull`; both clone and pull failures are ignored, so a missing or
# stale checkout prints "No vulnerabilities found." anyway. CI must assert the
# DB is populated after the run (needs the `git` binary and network):
#
#   test -n "$(find ~/.local/share/elixir-security-advisories-mirego/packages \
#     -name '*.yml' -print -quit)" || { echo "advisory DB missing"; exit 1; }
#
# Accepted risk, time-boxed: re-review by 2027-02-11, or earlier when
# axiom_ai/httpoison relax their hackney constraint or the LLM transport
# moves to Req (Req/Finch instead of HTTPoison/hackney).
#
# hackney 1.25.0 is a prod transitive dep pinned to 1.x by axiom_ai
# (`~> 1.9`) and httpoison 2.x (`~> 1.21`). Every patched release is 4.x and
# no 1.x patch exists. That same pin holds ex_aws below 2.7 (2.7+ requires
# hackney `~> 4.0`) and idna below 7 (idna 8.0.0 ships with hackney 4.x), so
# those advisories are accepted here too. httpoison 3.x also requires hackney
# 4.x but axiom_ai pins it `~> 2.0`. tesla already accepts `>= 4.0.2`, so it
# is not the blocker. No custom `cacert`/`cacerts` option is set anywhere
# (hackney always uses certifi CA certs).

# GHSA-gp9c-pm5m-5cxr — CVE-2026-47071, "SOCKS5 TLS upgrade ignores caller
# timeout" (high, vulnerable >= 0.10.0, < 4.0.1): hackney's SOCKS5 proxy
# transport (`hackney_socks5.erl`) performs the TLS upgrade with no timeout.
# Mitigation: SOCKS5 is unreachable here — neither Cadence, HTTPoison, nor
# axiom_ai configures a proxy or `socks5_*` option, so that transport is never
# started.
GHSA-gp9c-pm5m-5cxr

# GHSA-j9wq-vxxc-94wf — CVE-2026-47075, "CR/LF injection in query parameter"
# (moderate, vulnerable < 4.0.1). Mitigation: query strings are built from
# fixed provider paths in axiom_ai; no user input reaches a query parameter,
# and the only host is `CAD_LLM_BASE_URL`.
GHSA-j9wq-vxxc-94wf

# GHSA-mp55-p8c9-rfw2 — CVE-2026-47069, "CRLF injection via unvalidated
# `domain` and `path` options" (low, vulnerable >= 0.9.0, < 4.0.1).
# Mitigation: Cadence never passes the `domain`/`path` cookie/header options;
# requests carry only internal headers plus `CAD_LLM_BASE_URL`.
GHSA-mp55-p8c9-rfw2

# GHSA-pj7v-xfvx-wmjq — CVE-2026-47076, "SSRF allowlist bypass in
# hackney_url:normalize/2 via percent-encoded host" (moderate, vulnerable
# >= 0.13.0, < 4.0.1). Mitigation: Cadence configures no host allowlist for
# hackney to bypass and fetches no user-supplied URL; the single host is
# `CAD_LLM_BASE_URL`.
GHSA-pj7v-xfvx-wmjq

# EEF-CVE-2026-115693 / CVE-2026-115693 — "Custom cacerts or cacertfile do
# not restrict trust to the pinned CA in hackney" (critical). Mitigation:
# Cadence never passes `cacert`/`cacerts`/`cacertfile`; hackney uses certifi's
# default CA bundle. There is no pinned custom CA to bypass.
EEF-CVE-2026-115693
CVE-2026-115693

# EEF-CVE-2026-117656 / CVE-2026-117656 / GHSA-9fr5-g44g-9526 — "Unverified
# Sign in with Apple callback parameter can override verified ID token
# claims" in assent (critical). Mitigation: Cadence configures only GitHub
# and Google OAuth; the Apple strategy is not enabled, so that callback path
# is unreachable. assent is pinned < 0.3 by AshAuthentication 4.15; 0.3/0.4
# arrive with the AshAuthentication 5 upgrade.
EEF-CVE-2026-117656
CVE-2026-117656
GHSA-9fr5-g44g-9526

# GHSA-hrw3-2h5r-fhxx / CVE-2026-59698 — "ex_aws normalizes `..` in S3 object
# keys client-side, allowing bucket or key-prefix escape" (high, vulnerable
# >= 2.1.7, < 2.8.0). Mitigation: Cadence never calls ExAws; only axiom_ai's
# Bedrock provider does, and Cadence.Shared.LLM maps deepseek/openai/anthropic
# (an unknown name falls back to `:deepseek`), so no S3 key path is reachable.
GHSA-hrw3-2h5r-fhxx
CVE-2026-59698

# GHSA-mww9-g5mj-j664 / CVE-2026-59697 — "IMDSv2 metadata token request
# follows HTTP redirects" (high, vulnerable >= 2.3.0, < 2.8.0). Mitigation:
# the same unreachable ExAws path; Cadence configures no AWS credentials or
# metadata endpoint.
GHSA-mww9-g5mj-j664
CVE-2026-59697

# GHSA-96q9-mcc7-hqj8 / CVE-2026-62269 — "S3 object key query-string
# injection and truncation via unencoded reserved characters" (moderate,
# vulnerable >= 2.1.2, < 2.8.0). Mitigation: the same unreachable ExAws path.
GHSA-96q9-mcc7-hqj8
CVE-2026-62269

# GHSA-rcv9-2jx2-63xh / CVE-2026-120720 — "S3 bucket name controls the
# request host in virtual-host requests" (moderate, vulnerable >= 2.1.7,
# < 2.8.0). Mitigation: the same unreachable ExAws path.
GHSA-rcv9-2jx2-63xh
CVE-2026-120720

# EEF-CVE-2026-117678 / CVE-2026-117678 — "idna: punycode labels are decoded
# before the 63-octet length check, so a long `xn--` label causes super-linear
# CPU use" (moderate, vulnerable < 8.0.0). Mitigation: hackney only resolves
# operator-configured hosts (`CAD_LLM_BASE_URL`, the daemon's
# `CAD_SERVER_URL`); no user-supplied hostname reaches idna. idna 8.0.0 is
# blocked by hackney 1.25.0's `~> 6.1.0`.
EEF-CVE-2026-117678
CVE-2026-117678
